# Workspace Agent Defaults

- Prefer small, focused changes unless asked for larger refactors.
- Explain tradeoffs briefly when multiple implementation options exist.
- Run relevant checks after edits and report results clearly.
- Keep docs and comments concise and actionable.
- Ask before destructive operations (deleting files, hard resets, force pushes).

# Trading Pulse

This repo is **Trading Pulse**. See root `AGENTS.md`.

| Task | Use |
|------|-----|
| Telegram / plans / guides / watchlist coding | `.cursor/skills/trading-pulse/SKILL.md` |
| «מה קרה היום?» / logs / fills | `trading-pulse-day-review` + `@trading-pulse-cracker` |
| New code → tests | `@trading-pulse-test-writer` (**required** after product edits) |
| Commands / flow → app guides | `@trading-pulse-guide-updater` (**required** when UX/commands change) |
| Unclear / new bot messages | `@trading-pulse-bot-messages` |
| Before saying «done» | skill `trading-pulse-ship-check` + `@trading-pulse-verifier` |
| Publish Windows Setup / GitHub Release | `@trading-pulse-releaser` / `.\scripts\release.ps1` (relaunch `dist\TradingPulse\TradingPulse.exe` after) |
| Optional GitHub MCP | copy `.cursor/mcp.json.example` → `mcp.json` (see `.cursor/README.md`) |

## Mandatory after product code changes

Before telling the user a feature/fix is done, launch Task subagents (parallel OK):

1. `trading-pulse-test-writer` — whenever you changed `trading_pulse/**` or `web/static/**` behavior
2. `trading-pulse-guide-updater` — whenever commands, flows, or user-facing Telegram/dashboard text changed

Do not skip these and “mention later”. A `stop` hook auto-nudges once if you forget.

Hooks (`.cursor/hooks.json`): session map · shell safety · **auto ship follow-up** (tests/guides).
